{
	title: 'Model-written compaction checkpoints',
	spec: 'COMPACT accepts a nonempty model-written working-state summary through the native tool. It atomically replaces active provider context only after its tool exchange settles, preserves current user requests verbatim and current instructions, and continues the same session. Summary guidance covers user goals and unresolved requirements, decisions and facts versus hypotheses, changes and actual verification and blockers, a consistent next action, and recoverable file/history references. Prefer task boundaries and compact before further substantial work at 200k; 150k notices suggest the next sensible stopping point, with 250k reminder. Manual /compact [focus] asks the current model to use COMPACT without a separate summarizer; undo remains. Failed or canceled preparation leaves context intact. Store checkpoints and transition intents durably; preserve full transcript, original records and READ_ENTRY access, restart consistency and undo. Show the supplied summary in existing tool detail in both clients. Avoid automatic recent-tail selection, background summarization, file rehydration and provider-specific compaction. Keep existing model-free overflow recovery as emergency fallback. Tests cover native syntax, validation, settled exchanges, continued requests, original prompt preservation, cancellation, history and recovery. Replaces the no-model-summary default, not the immutable-history invariant.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'COMPACT uses the existing durable context-transition intent with a summary field; installation happens after tool results and crash recovery deduplicates by transition ID. Mixed tool rounds are refused because their outcomes are not yet known to the summary writer. Manual requests use the normal prompt scheduler, attributed to Hal with generatingCommand compact; fulfilled preparation text is omitted from kept provider prompts to prevent compaction loops, but remains in history. No additional model call or background job. Existing generic tool details expose the supplied summary in both clients.',
		'Current turn text requests and the latest substantive request stay verbatim. Notice-only records are not retained for model-written checkpoints; context nudges explicitly refer to the pre-compaction measurement to avoid stale-pressure loops. Overflow recovery still uses the old deterministic summary. Full history and existing undo/search/READ_ENTRY remain unchanged.',
